          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;"Look upon my works, ye mighty, and despair!"&lt;br /&gt;Catra is an agent in time, at the whim of a war that rages eternally without meaning.&lt;br /&gt;Adora is a killing machine running on empty, fed up with a temporal-galactic spree of violence.&lt;br /&gt;Catra leaves Adora a letter in the ruins of a battlefield, and Adora responds.&lt;br /&gt;The rest isn't history, but the future and past colliding.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>hazelspacecadet</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mature</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra &amp; Hordak (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora &amp; Angella (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Hordak (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angella (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Perfuma (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Frosta (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>F/F</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Graphic Depictions Of Violence</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Major Character Death</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Original Characters</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Alternate Universe - Time Travel</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Multiple Realities</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>original lore</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>various allusions to philosophy</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>read the conspiracy against the human race by thomas ligotti and this all makes more sense i promise</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>also hegel and stirner i guess</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Slow Burn</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>not even really a slow burn because its not that long but like kinda</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mean Lesbians</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>mean as in they kill people fr</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>This is How You Lose the Time War - Amal El-Mohtar &amp; Max Gladstone</rdf:li>
